# Regression for a stack-buffer-overflow found while implementing case/
# when: parse_if's before_types/then_types type-inference snapshots used
# to be fixed uint8_t[256]/int16_t[256] arrays indexed up to
# compiler->next_register with no bounds check, so any if/elsif/unless
# reached after more than 256 registers had already been allocated in the
# enclosing function body overflowed them (confirmed under ASan). This
# pushes the register count well past 256 via the same discarded-`x + x`
# idiom wide_register_function.di uses, then exercises an if/elsif/else
# chain (including the recursive elsif path) right where the overflow
# used to happen.
def wide_register_if_elsif(x)
  x + x
  x + x
  x + x
  x + x
  x + x
  x + x
  x + x
  x + x
  x + x
  x + x
  x + x
  x + x
  x + x
  x + x
  x + x
  x + x
  x + x
  x + x
  x + x
  x + x
  x + x
  x + x
